WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
In Halloween Ends, we see a Laurie Strode who&nbsp;
is trying to find some normalcy in her life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:07.980
She needs to overcome her past by celebrating&nbsp;
Halloween like a normal person, rather than going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:12.300
to war with Michael Myers. To do this, we see her&nbsp;
carve a pumpkin, a holiday activity she took part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:17.400
in when we first met her in 1978. Back then it was&nbsp;
her, Tommy and Lindsey, and this time she’s with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.360
Allyson and Lindsey. Later on we get a look at&nbsp;
the finished product, and it looks just like the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:25.920
one she carved all those years ago. I guess her&nbsp;
style hasn’t changed much over the last 44 years.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:30.360
We also see this in her attire. In the original&nbsp;
film, she had this long brim hat in her room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:34.500
which she held onto until 2018, where it would&nbsp;
have been destroyed in the fire. Ironically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:38.160
when she burns her pie in Halloween Ends, you&nbsp;
can spot a replacement hat near the front door.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.920
Another trait from Laurie’s past&nbsp;
that persevered is the way she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.320
twirls her hair when she thinks&nbsp;
about her crush. In the original,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:46.740
she did this while discussing the target&nbsp;
of her high school affection, Ben Tramer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:51.480
and now, 44 years later, she reacts similarly when&nbsp;
running into Frank Hawkins at the supermarket.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.080
Maybe you didn’t notice those details when&nbsp;
you first watched the movie, so in this video&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:59.580
I’m gonna go over everything you might have&nbsp;
missed in Halloween Ends, from tiny details in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:04.020
newspapers to the broader meaning of the entire&nbsp;
film. Stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:06.540
This video is brought to&nbsp;
you by Established Titles.

00:01:06.657 --> 00:01:10.746
(metal music)

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:17.040
Welcome to Things You Missed. We once again&nbsp;
find ourselves at the end of the line here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.420
on the Halloween Express. I’m glad to see one of&nbsp;
these timelines actually have a definitive ending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:25.260
for once. You could argue that Rob Zombie’s&nbsp;
timeline was definitive, but Halloween Ends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:29.160
leaves little to the imagination. No matter what&nbsp;
you think about this movie, you have to give the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:33.300
filmmaker David Gordon Green and writer Danny&nbsp;
McBride credit for finishing what they started.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.700
Every good story has a beginning, middle and end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:40.200
even when it does include a timeless character&nbsp;
like Michael Myers. This story has come to an end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.980
but like every great legend, it can alway&nbsp;
be reimagined for future generations.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:47.400
While the story may have come to an end,&nbsp;
there are still many more Things You might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:51.000
have Missed to slash our way though,&nbsp;
so let’s slide in to our next one.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:57.065
(50s rock)

00:01:57.065 --> 00:02:00.420
The opening song of the movie, “Midnight&nbsp;
Monsters Hop” has lyrics that describe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:04.140
a concert with many classic Halloween&nbsp;
monsters like Dracula, The Invisible Man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:08.820
Frankenstein and the Mummy, who started as pop&nbsp;
culture icons, like Michael Myers, but are now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:13.560
eternal urban legends. These are classic Universal&nbsp;
monsters, and this trilogy of Halloween films was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:18.000
made by Universal’s Blumhouse, so it’s almost as&nbsp;
if Michael Myers is following in their footsteps.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.120
The opening titles are done in the same&nbsp;
style as the titles from Halloween III:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:24.780
Season of the Witch, the black sheep of the&nbsp;
franchise. This made me realize that there’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:28.800
a pattern. Halloween (2018) was the first&nbsp;
Blumhouse Halloween, and it mimics the titles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.180
from Halloween 1. Halloween Kills was the second&nbsp;
Blumhouse Halloween and its titles resemble Rick’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:37.560
Halloween 2. Ends is the third of the Blumhouse&nbsp;
trilogy, so it took the style of Halloween III.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:41.700
The opening scene shows our new character Corey&nbsp;
babysitting for this kid named Jeremy. As the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:45.360
parents are about to leave, I noticed the mom&nbsp;
holding a small drone. It reminded me of that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.900
scene from Halloween Kills, where Michael&nbsp;
destroys Sonda’s drone, before attacking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:52.440
her and her husband. But I don’t think this&nbsp;
drone is a callback, because shortly after,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:57.360
we see that Jeremy prefers playing with paper&nbsp;
airplanes. He has access to the newest technology,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.720
but still chooses the old classic. We&nbsp;
also see Laurie playing with a paper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:05.460
plane when she confronts Corey later on. It seems&nbsp;
symbolic for a movie with two main antagonists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:09.420
the old classic, Michael Myers, and the&nbsp;
newcomer, Corey Cunningham. Corey just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:13.376
ends up modeling himself after Michael,&nbsp;
so once again, the original can’t be beat.

00:03:13.376 --> 00:03:16.320
– It’s Halloween. We’re gonna&nbsp;
have a good time tonight.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:20.160
– Thank God he didn’t say everyone’s entitled&nbsp;
to one good scare. Corey and Jeremy end up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:23.460
watching John Carpenter’s The Thing, which&nbsp;
is a remake of The Thing From Another World,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:25.200
which Laurie and Tommy watched in the original.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.960
It’s significant that they chose&nbsp;
John Carpenter’s The Thing because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:30.540
as you may know, John Carpenter&nbsp;
directed the original Halloween,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:34.080
and Halloween Ends honors more of&nbsp;
his filmography. In particular,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:39.300
Ends is more of a remake of John Carpenter’s 1983&nbsp;
film Christine than it is a Halloween sequel.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:43.260
In Halloween Ends, we follow a character named&nbsp;
Corey Cunningham, who is an obvious homage to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:47.280
Christine’s main character, Arnie Cunningham.&nbsp;
Spoilers for Christine until the end of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:51.960
chapter. Arnie starts off as kind of a loser until&nbsp;
he buys this old car named Christine and decides&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:55.920
to fix it up. As he does so, he becomes cooler&nbsp;
and starts to stand up for himself against his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:00.180
bullies and his overly strict parents. The&nbsp;
car is actually a supernatural entity with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:04.260
the ability to repair herself and go after&nbsp;
Arnie’s enemies on her own. Owning this car&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:08.820
changes his personality and grows his ego, but&nbsp;
it goes too far, and Arnie becomes a villain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:12.060
willing to attack those who care about him&nbsp;
when they show concern about the evil car.

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:16.680
In Halloween Ends, Corey starts as an outcast&nbsp;
because of his babysitting accident. Like Arnie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:20.760
he gets his glasses broken by high school bullies,&nbsp;
and his life is dominated by his strict mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:24.240
but his luck starts to change when he&nbsp;
receives this motorcycle from his step dad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:28.440
with the promise that he can fix it up. Corey&nbsp;
works at Prevo Auto, which looks like a smaller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:32.880
version of Darnell’s Garage where Arnie fixes up&nbsp;
Christine. I found it interesting that Prevo Auto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:37.860
was established in 1963, the same year Michael&nbsp;
seemingly became evil and killed his older sister.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:41.760
It’s like there’s this parallel between Michael&nbsp;
and the junkyard, which is appropriate because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:46.740
Corey’s motorcycle is not the “Christine” of this&nbsp;
movie. Michael Myers is Christine. Let me explain.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:51.480
Corey is always said to be a good kid who had a&nbsp;
bad break. Even the father of the boy he killed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:55.440
admits that Jeremy’s death was an accident, but&nbsp;
something else later seemed to send Corey down a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:59.280
dark path. It is true that this happens right&nbsp;
after he gets the motorcycle, but it’s around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:03.600
this same time that he first encounters Michael&nbsp;
Myers. Like Christine, Michael Myers is in a sad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:07.920
state when we first encounter him, and Corey, like&nbsp;
Arnie, develops a strange fascination with him.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:11.580
Christine seems to have Arnie under some kind&nbsp;
of trance as soon as he lays eyes on her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:15.240
and Halloween Ends features this moment where&nbsp;
Corey and Michael first make eye contact and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:19.500
something non-verbal seems to be passed between&nbsp;
them. Christine seems to regain her power after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:23.640
Arnie spends countless hours fixing her up in the&nbsp;
garage, and in Michael’s case, he seems to regain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:27.360
power after Corey brings him a new victim.&nbsp;
The way Christine puts herself back together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:31.680
even kind of resembles the way that Michael&nbsp;
visually regains his mojo after taking a life.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:35.760
In each film, the Cunningham character gains&nbsp;
more confidence and swagger after their first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:38.340
encounter with the supernatural.&nbsp;
They both ditch their glasses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:41.160
because not wearing glasses instantly&nbsp;
makes you more attractive in a movie.

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:43.860
– Hey man, no glasses. You’re looking good.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:47.640
– Arnie Cunningham starts dating the most coveted&nbsp;
girl in the school, and Christine tries to kill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:51.660
her by locking her in the cabin when she starts&nbsp;
choking. Corey Cunningham meets and begins to date&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:56.100
Allyson, who is similarly an enemy of Michael.&nbsp;
Arnie stops listening to his mother and stops&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.100 --> 00:06:00.420
respecting his parents, and Corey does the same.&nbsp;
Finally, Christine is totalled by bullies, so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:04.800
after getting fixed, she goes after them and hunts&nbsp;
them down. Each time, we see the bright headlights&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:08.700
blasting them before Christine chases them down&nbsp;
and kills them. In Halloween, the bullies try&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:12.240
to ruin Corey’s motorcycle, and he confronts them&nbsp;
by targeting them in the bright lights of the tow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:16.620
truck before running them down. It's definitely&nbsp;
paying tribute to that iconic Christine shot.

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:20.880
In the end, Arnie’s best friend and ex-girlfriend&nbsp;
battle and defeat Christine in the auto garage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:23.040
where she’s compacted and dumped in the junkyard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:26.880
but they are unable to save Arnie. While&nbsp;
in Halloween Ends, Laurie and Allyson also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:31.020
defeat Michael and bring him to the junkyard to&nbsp;
be destroyed, but they are unable to save Corey.

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:35.040
There’s also a cameo in this movie from Diana&nbsp;
Prince, who is known in the horror community as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:39.360
co-host of The Last Drive-In. One of Chrstine’s&nbsp;
iconic scenes takes place at a drive-in movie.

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:42.900
There was talk earlier this year of&nbsp;
Christine getting its own Blumhouse remake,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:47.220
which Stephen King, the author of the novel, was&nbsp;
not thrilled about, so I’m hoping Halloween Ends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:51.540
is instead of that, because I think I prefer&nbsp;
this weird amalgamation of two John Carpenter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:55.980
movies to a remake of a movie that still holds&nbsp;
up, and doesn’t really need to be remade. Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.980 --> 00:06:58.800
Stephen King liked it -- seriously&nbsp;
Blumhouse, quit while you’re ahead.

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:03.060
After meeting Corey, we move on to Laurie, who&nbsp;
has a collection of newspapers pinned to her wall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:05.340
which contain a few Things You might have Missed.

