00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:22.260
(mysterious music)

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:26.160
One thing Halloween Ends does really well&nbsp;
is foreshadowing, which makes it a joy to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:29.880
watch for your second and third viewing. There&nbsp;
are many covert clues about Corey’s transition&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:33.540
to evil and alignment with Michael Myers.&nbsp;
In my Michael Myers Horror History episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:37.740
I talked all about how Michael seems to be stuck&nbsp;
in a childlike mindset because of his trauma at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:41.640
six years old. Corey seems to have that same&nbsp;
mindset, which can be seen in his beverage of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:45.540
choice. In the opening he’s confronted with a&nbsp;
choice between chocolate milk and beer and he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:49.560
goes with chocolate milk. Then again at the gas&nbsp;
station, he chooses milk, and refuses to buy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:53.820
beer for the kids pressuring him in the parking&nbsp;
lot. Beer is obviously an adult beverage, you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:58.020
have to be 21 to drink it in the US; while milk&nbsp;
is considered beneficial for growing children,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.020 --> 00:09:03.000
but the lactase enzyme responsible for digesting&nbsp;
it goes away in most adults. I also noticed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:07.140
Corey’s mom drinks milk with her spaghetti,&nbsp;
and she definitely has some weird issues.

00:09:07.140 --> 00:09:11.880
Another example of foreshadowing can be seen in&nbsp;
Corey’s actual shadow as he heads up the stairs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:16.020
It looks like the silhouette of Michael&nbsp;
Myers, which we saw before in Halloween 6.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:19.620
As I mentioned, Corey is a mechanic, and&nbsp;
we see him in his work uniform early on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:24.240
which happens to be the same costume that Michael&nbsp;
Myers wears. He’s also seen using the blow torch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:28.020
which he would later weaponize against the leader&nbsp;
of the bullies, Terry, in a pretty awesome kill.

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:32.100
When Corey and Allyson hang out on the rooftop of&nbsp;
the radio station, he claims he’s not interested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:35.940
in immortality, and drops down to the ground,&nbsp;
falling on his back. He appears to be hurt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:39.900
then sits up in the same fashion that Michael&nbsp;
always sits up after a recharge period.

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:43.740
Corey’s death, or at least his apparent&nbsp;
death, is also foreshadowed during the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.740 --> 00:09:46.980
dance party scene. He’s laying on the&nbsp;
dance floor for some reason and Allyson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:50.520
runs her hands along his face and neck.&nbsp;
At the end, when Allyson comes home to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:53.700
discover Corey’s self-inflicted injury,&nbsp;
she finds herself in the same position.

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:57.180
Outside of hints about Corey, there are&nbsp;
also other aspects of the movie that are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.180 --> 00:10:00.900
set up. The recap at the beginning uses a&nbsp;
shot from the original Halloween of Laurie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:04.020
attacking Michael with her knitting needle.&nbsp;
Most of us have seen the original Halloween,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.020 --> 00:10:07.380
but it's a nice touch to include that for&nbsp;
those who haven’t, because it foreshadows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:10.800
the moment later in Halloween Ends.&nbsp;
We even see that she still knits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:14.280
so it makes more sense when she finds the needle&nbsp;
and uses it as a weapon in the final battle.

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:17.640
There are many aspects of the final&nbsp;
showdown that are set up earlier on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:21.240
like the scene where Laurie burns her pumpkin&nbsp;
pie. This shows us the location of the fire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:25.500
extinguisher, so it’s more satisfying when she&nbsp;
gets it and uses it in the finale. Similarly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:28.560
there’s a scene where Allyson leaves her&nbsp;
meal in the microwave for too long and it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:32.280
explodes. Laurie later does this on purpose&nbsp;
as a loud noise that can distract Michael.

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:33.240
(food pops)

00:10:33.240 --> 00:10:37.260
Then, when Laurie tries to warn her granddaughter&nbsp;
about Corey, she uses the following words:

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:40.680
– I’m not gonna let this happen&nbsp;
to you, you have to believe me.

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:44.460
– …which are the first words out of Allyson’s mouth&nbsp;
when she comes back to save her grandmother.

00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:46.140
– I’m not gonna let this happen to you.

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:49.380
– And the last thing I’m going to point out as&nbsp;
far as foreshadowing, is how they foreshadowed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:53.460
Michael’s death. One of the first things we ever&nbsp;
see at the junkyard is that industrial shredder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:56.400
it’s very brief, but it’s a nice&nbsp;
setup. It’s shown again later on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:58.740
but my favorite might be the&nbsp;
butcher at the grocery store.

00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:02.435
– Three pound ground chuck. Right here on top.

00:11:02.435 --> 00:11:05.940
– Is that a little clue that Michael is going&nbsp;
to eventually become “ground beef” himself?

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:09.960
The procession scene right before Michael’s&nbsp;
body is destroyed is a great way to wrap up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:12.960
the trilogy, because it allows up to see&nbsp;
many of the characters who made it all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:16.560
the way through, like Sheriff Barker,&nbsp;
the graveyard caretaker Sondra Larsen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:20.400
and the snarky kid Julilan Morrisey. Each&nbsp;
of these characters appeared in all three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:25.140
movies and survived to the end. We even&nbsp;
see WCZD make one last appearance. Nice.

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:29.940
Let’s move on to the easter eggs. Some Halloween&nbsp;
fans may remember the Halloween novelizations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:33.480
These books were not canon, but gave fans a&nbsp;
little bit more detail about their favorite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:37.140
Halloween stories, characters and lore.&nbsp;
The novelization of the original Halloween&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.140 --> 00:11:40.860
has details about what became of Judith and&nbsp;
Michael’s parents after losing their kids,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.860 --> 00:11:45.480
where they are given names for the first time:&nbsp;
Donald Myers and Edith Myers. These names are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:49.740
referenced in Halloween Ends, in an article pinned&nbsp;
to Laurie Strode’s wall titled “6 Year Old Kills&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:53.940
Teen Sister in Halloween Tragedy”. You can see&nbsp;
their names from the novelization are now canon.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:56.940
There’s also an Obituaries section&nbsp;
revealing the name of Lynda’s mother:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.940 --> 00:12:00.595
Marlyn Van Der Klok. This is also&nbsp;
a name taken from the novelization.

00:12:00.595 --> 00:12:05.400
Then again, you might not want to trust the&nbsp;
newspapers. This article titled “Myers Manhunt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:10.620
Underway” states that Michael had 27 victims&nbsp;
in 2018. It’s not entirely clear who lived and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:14.460
who died, but if you tally up the victims&nbsp;
from Halloween (2018) and Halloween Kills,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:18.600
you would get a number somewhere in the fifties. I&nbsp;
like to think this article was written before all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:21.780
the bodies had been discovered, but there’s&nbsp;
no excuse you can make for this next part,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:26.100
where it says in 1978, Michael killed&nbsp;
5 teenagers with Laurie Strode being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:30.660
the only sole survivor. This is just not&nbsp;
true. Michael killed 3 teenagers that year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:34.680
and Laurie was one of four survivors,&nbsp;
alongside Tommy, Lindsey, and Dr. Loomis.

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:38.100
There’s one more potential error here,&nbsp;
where it says Michael was last seen at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:41.280
45 Lampkin Lane in Haddonfield.&nbsp;
In my Halloween Kills episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:45.780
I talked about how the address of the Myers&nbsp;
house is 709 Lampkin Lane, with 45 Lampkin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:49.920
Lane being a mistake made in Rick’s Halloween&nbsp;
II, which is not a part of this timeline. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:53.460
is possible though, that there’s a neighbor&nbsp;
who actually does live at 45 Lampkin Lane,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:57.060
who was the last one to spot Michael. Maybe&nbsp;
that’s what the article is talking about.

00:12:57.060 --> 00:13:00.420
As long as we’re taking a closer look at&nbsp;
these articles, let’s look at this one:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:04.080
“Night Blade Landmark Destroyed.” Night&nbsp;
Blade was a working title for Halloween&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:07.920
(2018) during the early stages of production&nbsp;
and the film was made under the company name:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:11.640
Night Blade Holdings LLC. Kills&nbsp;
followed suit with the company&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:15.780
name being Night Blade 2 Holdings, and&nbsp;
Ends was made by Night Blade 3 Holdings.

00:13:15.780 --> 00:13:19.980
But this article was not the only instance&nbsp;
of the behind-the-scenes content being in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:23.400
the scenes themselves. This hobo&nbsp;
is a cameo by Christopher Nelson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:26.400
the special makeup effects designer&nbsp;
for the trilogy. You may remember I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:30.060
pointed out his other cameo in Halloween&nbsp;
(2018), where he played a police officer.

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:34.560
Debra Hill, who produced on the original three&nbsp;
Halloween movies, is sadly no longer around to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:38.400
make a cameo appearance, but there is a nurse&nbsp;
character named Deb who seems to be a tribute&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:42.420
to her. During the production of the original&nbsp;
Halloween, she was dating John Carpenter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:45.420
and the character Deb is secretly dating&nbsp;
the man calling the shots at the clinic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:50.820
Dr. Mathis. Of course, Deb’s death is a direct&nbsp;
retread of a famous death from the original movie.

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:54.780
Throughout Halloween Ends, Laurie can be seen&nbsp;
writing a book in order to help her cope with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.780 --> 00:13:59.040
horrible events she has endured. This is almost&nbsp;
certainly a nod to her fellow final girl Sidney&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:03.720
Prescott, who has a similar coping strategy in&nbsp;
Scre4m. Yes, that is the correct pronunciation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:09.060
based on the spelling, Scre-4-m. The relationship&nbsp;
between Halloween and Scream began in 1996,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:09.060 --> 00:14:13.800
in the original Scream, where Halloween was shown&nbsp;
to guests at a party. In 1998, Halloween H20&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:18.960
showed Scream 2 on a dorm room TV. Then in 2000,&nbsp;
Scream 3 has a scene where Sidney’s mother says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:22.500
she’ll protect her from The Boogeyman, which is&nbsp;
a name that is interchangeable with Michael Myers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:26.940
in the Halloween franchise. In Scre4m, Sidney is&nbsp;
introduced as the ultimate scream queen beyond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:31.080
Jamie Lee Curtis, the actress who plays Laurie,&nbsp;
among a variety of other references, so I believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:31.080 --> 00:14:34.440
Laurie’s transformation into a self-help&nbsp;
author is a reference to the fourth Scream.

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:37.329
Her book is titled Stalkers, Saviors and Samhain…

00:14:37.329 --> 00:14:38.263
– [Loomis and Zac] Sam Hain.

00:14:38.263 --> 00:14:41.940
– [Zac] Samhain is the Gaelic festival marking the&nbsp;
end of the harvest season in Celtic Ireland,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:43.980
which was a big part of the lore in Halloween 2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:48.000
3 and 6. You can watch my episodes on each&nbsp;
of those movies if you want to know more,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:52.080
but the appearance here on Laurie’s book title is&nbsp;
an easter egg waiting to be noticed by fans of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.080 --> 00:14:56.160
originals. There’s another reference to Celtic&nbsp;
Folklore in the song that the homeless man sings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.160 --> 00:15:00.120
after Corey is thrown off the overpass. You’ve&nbsp;
gotta listen pretty carefully to pick up on it.

00:15:01.826 --> 00:15:07.080
– ♪ There's a hole in the boat ♪
♪ And it won't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:12.602
stay afloat ♪
♪ Oilliphéist in the sea ♪

00:15:12.602 --> 00:15:17.160
– If you couldn’t hear that, he says: There's a hole&nbsp;
in the boat. And it won't stay afloat. Oilliphéist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:21.600
in the sea. This song is called “Oilliphéist,&nbsp;
Fear Thee”. The Oilliphéist is a mythological sea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:26.040
serpent creature originating in Irish Mythology.&nbsp;
The rest of his song may also be significant.

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:31.800
– ♪ Nail my hands to the door ♪
♪ And my knees to the floor ♪

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:35.040
– At the end of the movie, Michael’s hands&nbsp;
are nailed down with knives and his knees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:38.400
are trapped down by the refrigerator,&nbsp;
so this line might be connected to that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:42.180
But there are still a ton more easter eggs&nbsp;
referencing other films in the franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:42.180 --> 00:15:46.920
and I’m gonna talk about how Halloween Ends has&nbsp;
a message about COVID-19 and what the director&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:51.240
meant when he said that Haddonfield is going to&nbsp;
be dealing with the pandemic in Halloween Ends.

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:53.974
(impact)

00:15:56.536 --> 00:16:00.542
(mysterious music)

00:16:00.542 --> 00:16:03.600
There’s a four year gap in between&nbsp;
the end of Halloween Kills and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:06.420
main events of Halloween Ends,&nbsp;
during which Allyson graduates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:06.420 --> 00:16:10.800
gets a job and starts dating a police officer&nbsp;
named Doug Mulaney. This character is most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:14.317
likely a descendent of the Mulaneys&nbsp;
from the flashback in Halloween Kills.

00:16:14.317 --> 00:16:15.060
– That’s what you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:16.560
get when you **** with the Mulaneys.

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:19.020
– Looks like their family motto&nbsp;
got passed down as well.

00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:22.217
– Hey! You don’t **** with Doug Mulaney!

00:16:22.217 --> 00:16:25.680
– I gotta admit, I spent way too long&nbsp;
trying to figure out who the Mulaneys&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:28.680
were supposed to be in Kills, and did&nbsp;
not consider it might be a set up for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:31.800
next movie. Another connection to Kills&nbsp;
can be seen right here in the graffiti,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:36.120
which reads “love lives today”, the same text&nbsp;
seen on the donation box back at Mick’s Bar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:39.147
which helped inspire everybody’s&nbsp;
favorite line from that middle chapter.

00:16:39.147 --> 00:16:42.720
– [Tommy] Love lives today.
– [Marion] But evil dies tonight.

00:16:42.720 --> 00:16:47.880
–  [Zac] Next to the “love lives today” graffiti is just&nbsp;
the word “KILLS” incase we forgot the name of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:51.540
the previous title, and there’s also some&nbsp;
artwork of Michael Myers, which might be of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:55.740
note because the police procession goes down this&nbsp;
same street before Michael’s execution at the end.

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:59.760
And speaking of the ending, it also has a&nbsp;
couple of Halloween Kills references. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:59.760 --> 00:17:03.240
pinning Michael to the kitchen island, Laurie&nbsp;
shows him his own reflection in the knife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:03.240 --> 00:17:06.106
probably to test Deputy Hawkins’s&nbsp;
theory from the last movie.

00:17:06.106 --> 00:17:12.300
– [Hawkins] Maybe he wasn’t looking out. Maybe&nbsp;
he was looking in. At his reflection. At himself.

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:15.240
– And when Michael gets the upper hand she yells “do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:15.240 --> 00:17:18.120
it!” in a way that almost looks like&nbsp;
she’s encouraging him to kill her.

00:17:18.120 --> 00:17:21.497
– Do it. Do it!

00:17:21.497 --> 00:17:25.800
– Of course, she’s really talking to Allyson, is&nbsp;
standing behind Michael and comes to rescue her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:29.700
This mirrors the scene in Kills where Allyson&nbsp;
is at Michael’s mercy and yells “do it!”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:33.000
but she’s really talking to her mother who&nbsp;
is standing at the door with a pitchfork.

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:36.840
I find it interesting that in order to stop&nbsp;
Michael, Laurie pins him down to the kitchen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:40.440
island, because in Halloween (2018) she&nbsp;
had set up a much more elaborate trap&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:40.440 --> 00:17:44.400
for him under her kitchen island, but the&nbsp;
simpler trap ends up being more effective.

00:17:44.400 --> 00:17:48.600
Halloween (2018) also shares another&nbsp;
similar line with Ends. At one point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:52.260
Corey comes over to visit Allyson late at&nbsp;
night, and he’s extremely flustered. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:55.740
tries to calm him down by saying “look&nbsp;
at me”, the same tactic her mother once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:55.740 --> 00:17:59.220
used to try to calm down Laurie during her&nbsp;
panic attack at the honors society dinner.

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:01.080
– [Allyson] Look at me.
– [Karen] Mom, look at me.

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:04.440
– Another (2018) connection is visible&nbsp;
when Allyson pulls up to the restaurant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:04.440 --> 00:18:08.580
she’s meeting Corey at. The sign out front&nbsp;
advertises Bahn Mi sandwiches, the same type&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:08.580 --> 00:18:12.354
of sandwich that the cop stationed outside of&nbsp;
Laurie’s house was raving out four years prior.

00:18:12.354 --> 00:18:18.180
– A bahn mi sandwich. A bahn mi is essentially&nbsp;
just a Vietnamese version of a French baguette.

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:20.940
– Outside of the 40 year trilogy,&nbsp;
there are still plenty of other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:20.940 --> 00:18:23.820
Halloween easter eggs to uncover. I’ll&nbsp;
start with Halloween Resurrection,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:23.820 --> 00:18:27.360
and we can work our way backwards. When we&nbsp;
first see Michael’s new home in the sewers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:27.360 --> 00:18:30.600
there’s an insert shot of the rats, which&nbsp;
brings to mind Michael’s lair in Resurrection,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:30.600 --> 00:18:33.420
where he lived underneath the house&nbsp;
and fed on rats for sustenance.

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:37.800
In Halloween H20, there was a tense scene where&nbsp;
the character Charlie drops a corkscrew into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:40.740
garbage disposal, and Michael sneaks&nbsp;
up on him as he’s reaching in for it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:40.740 --> 00:18:44.040
making it seem as if the boogeyman is going&nbsp;
to flip the switch to grind up Charlie’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:47.700
hand. That doesn’t end up happening, but when&nbsp;
Michael tries to force Laurie’s hand into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:50.880
garbage disposal in Halloween Ends,&nbsp;
it’s clearly an homage to that scene.

00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:53.940
There’s also a part where Laurie holds&nbsp;
onto Michael’s hand after trapping him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:57.180
which reminded me a lot of the ending&nbsp;
of H20, where the masked man is trapped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:57.180 --> 00:19:00.360
under a van and reaches out to Laurie,&nbsp;
where they briefly touch fingertips.

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:03.960
This movie also features a radio host&nbsp;
getting massacred during a broadcast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:03.960 --> 00:19:08.640
which we saw with Barry Simms in Halloween 6;&nbsp;
a retaliation from an angry driver of a black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:08.640 --> 00:19:13.260
convertible that got scratched, which we saw with&nbsp;
Mikey in Halloween 5; an adult giving a teenager&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:13.260 --> 00:19:17.520
a loaded rifle and telling him to stay put, which&nbsp;
we saw with Sheriff Meeker and Brady in Halloween&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:17.520 --> 00:19:22.860
4 and a tow-truck being stolen for a murderous&nbsp;
rampage, as we saw Michael do in Halloween 4.

00:19:22.860 --> 00:19:27.180
As always, we get a ton of connections to&nbsp;
the immortal classic, the 1978 original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:30.600
Halloween. It starts when Laurie is&nbsp;
talking to Hawkins in the supermarket,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:34.320
where you can hear the grocery store cover of&nbsp;
“[Don’t Fear] The Reaper” by Blue Öyster Cult.

00:19:34.492 --> 00:19:40.550
[muzak version of "(Don't Fear) The Reaper"]

00:19:40.550 --> 00:19:42.420
They must have watched my CHUCKY season 1 video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:42.420 --> 00:19:46.500
where I ranted about how I don’t dislike the&nbsp;
song, but it’s way overused in movies and TV,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:50.460
because they proceeded to put it twice in this&nbsp;
movie, it also plays over the end credits.

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:54.240
That evening when Allyson and Corey go to&nbsp;
the dance party, Corey bumps into this man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:58.740
played by Nick Castle, the actor under the Michael&nbsp;
Myers mask in the original, and also parts of 2018&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:58.740 --> 00:20:03.454
and Kills. This easter egg is actually a two&nbsp;
parter, because he opens his jacket and asks…

00:20:03.454 --> 00:20:05.301
– See anything you like?

00:20:05.301 --> 00:20:09.300
– …which is the same line Lynda had in the original&nbsp;
movie when flashing her tits to her boyfriend.

00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:11.498
– See anything you like?

00:20:11.498 --> 00:20:14.100
Corey goes off on his own, where&nbsp;
he’s jumped by the gang of bullies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:16.800
and tossed from the overpass. You can&nbsp;
see Michael Myers in the background&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:19.620
for just a moment, before we pan&nbsp;
down to see that Corey is alive.

00:20:19.620 --> 00:20:23.700
Laurie first sees Corey’s behavior start to change&nbsp;
when she notices him peering out from behind the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:27.060
bush in the front yard. This isn’t really&nbsp;
a Thing You Missed, because the shot in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:27.060 --> 00:20:30.840
original is so iconic, but people will complain&nbsp;
if I don’t mention it. A better one to bring up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:30.840 --> 00:20:34.380
would be that night, when Laurie comes home to&nbsp;
see Allyson and Corey heading up to the bedroom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:38.100
through the front window. In the original, it was&nbsp;
the young Michael Myers who caught a glimpse of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:38.100 --> 00:20:41.760
his sister leading her boyfriend upstairs.&nbsp;
This is a continuation of the trend that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:45.780
I talked about when covering Halloween (2018)&nbsp;
and Halloween Kills, where we are increasingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:45.780 --> 00:20:49.140
seeing the roles reversed between Laurie and&nbsp;
Michael, to where she is becoming the hunter.

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:53.580
Another detail I discussed in my (2018) video&nbsp;
was Allyson’s outfit starting to look like the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:57.300
wardrobe that Laurie wore in the original, and&nbsp;
we see that again here in the radio tower scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:57.300 --> 00:21:01.380
where she’s wearing that very familiar blue&nbsp;
button up and jeans. We also see Laurie wearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:01.380 --> 00:21:04.680
pretty much the same thing in the finale.&nbsp;
She first knows that Michael is back when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:08.220
she notices the open back door, which probably&nbsp;
reminded her of the window he came in through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:08.220 --> 00:21:12.720
in ‘78. As she did back then, she hides in a&nbsp;
closet, where she formulates a plan of attack.

00:21:12.720 --> 00:21:16.920
The very ending shows an array of still&nbsp;
shots all around Laurie’s house. It’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:21.180
just like the ending of the original Halloween,&nbsp;
but this time with no ominous breathing sounds.

00:21:21.180 --> 00:21:24.540
I’ve already brought up a few details you might&nbsp;
have missed from the Halloween Ends’s soundtrack,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:29.340
so here are a couple more. The second song we&nbsp;
hear at the dance party is “Halloween” by Dead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:29.340 --> 00:21:32.400
Kennedys, whose lyrics mention a character&nbsp;
who dressed up like a clown for Halloween.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:32.400 --> 00:21:37.080
Maybe this is a coincidence, but Michael’s first&nbsp;
costume in the first movie was a clown costume,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:40.140
and there have been many clown costume&nbsp;
appearances in other Halloween movies.

00:21:40.140 --> 00:21:44.880
There are a couple other songs that reflect ideas&nbsp;
expressed in the movie, like when Dr. Mathis gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:44.880 --> 00:21:49.320
home and puts on the song “Tell Me With Your Eyes”&nbsp;
by Rob Galbraith. Eyes are often depicted in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:54.180
movie to be indicators of good or evil. Laurie&nbsp;
says she can see Michael in Corey’s eyes. Roger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:54.180 --> 00:21:57.780
the father of the boy who got killed, also&nbsp;
says that when he looked into Corey’s eyes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:57.780 --> 00:22:00.960
he could tell he was down a dark&nbsp;
path. When Corey first meets Michael,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:04.920
they make eye contact, and something seems&nbsp;
to be passed between, during which we see a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:08.100
montage that includes a bunch of extreme&nbsp;
close ups of Corey and Michael’s eyes.

00:22:08.100 --> 00:22:11.820
Another more overt music choice&nbsp;
is “Burn it Down” by Boy Harsher,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:11.820 --> 00:22:14.760
which we hear when Corey and Allyson are&nbsp;
night riding on the motorcycle. This is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:14.760 --> 00:22:17.986
reference to the conversation they had about&nbsp;
their desires to get away from Haddonfield.

00:22:17.986 --> 00:22:21.900
– [Allyson] After my mom and dad were&nbsp;
killed I just wanted to burn it all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:23.580
to the ground and get away from Haddonfield.

00:22:23.580 --> 00:22:25.740
– They bring up this phrase a&nbsp;
few more times throughout the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:25.740 --> 00:22:28.020
rest of the runtime whenever they&nbsp;
are talking about skipping town,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:28.020 --> 00:22:32.640
and this motorcycle scene takes place right before&nbsp;
Corey finally convinces her to head out with him.

00:22:32.640 --> 00:22:36.720
But what is the deal with that piano melody that&nbsp;
characters keep playing over and over throughout&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:36.720 --> 00:22:41.340
the film? To answer that, we’ll have to look&nbsp;
back many years to one legendary composer.

00:22:41.340 --> 00:22:46.200
(impact)

00:22:46.496 --> 00:22:50.363
(dark music)

00:22:50.488 --> 00:22:53.040
We first hear Mr. Allen perform “Toccata and Fugue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:53.040 --> 00:22:57.000
in D Minor” by Johann Sebastian Bach in&nbsp;
the opening sequence on Halloween night.

00:22:57.131 --> 00:23:01.774
(piano music)

00:23:01.774 --> 00:23:05.160
This music choice makes sense, because&nbsp;
this song is most commonly associated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:05.160 --> 00:23:09.000
with the classic vampire film, Nosferatu.&nbsp;
Which, if you watch Things You Missed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:09.000 --> 00:23:12.960
you already know is where Michael Myers got&nbsp;
his creepy sit up move from. Remember how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:12.960 --> 00:23:16.020
I talked about Corey’s shadow on the&nbsp;
staircase looking like Michael Myers?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:16.020 --> 00:23:20.280
That also comes from Nosferatu, which&nbsp;
helped inspire many films to this day.

00:23:20.280 --> 00:23:23.340
We hear these iconic notes&nbsp;
repeated throughout Halloween Ends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:23.340 --> 00:23:25.791
when Allyson first enters&nbsp;
the abandoned Allen house…

00:23:25.791 --> 00:23:28.281
(piano keys)

00:23:28.281 --> 00:23:30.636
 …when Corey lets Laurie&nbsp;
Strode slip away…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:30.636 --> 00:23:33.540
(piano keys)

00:23:33.540 --> 00:23:37.776
and non-diegetically when Michael&nbsp;
comes across Laurie’s new house. 

00:23:37.776 --> 00:23:38.880
(piano notes)

00:23:38.880 --> 00:23:42.180
If you were following updates throughout&nbsp;
the production of Halloween Ends, you may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:42.180 --> 00:23:45.900
remember David Gordon-Green talking about&nbsp;
how the time jump in between Halloween Kills&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:45.900 --> 00:23:50.040
and Ends meant that Halloween Ends would&nbsp;
take place during the COVID-19 pandemic.

00:23:50.040 --> 00:23:54.180
In an October 2021 interview with Uproxx, he&nbsp;
stated: “Not only do they have their immediate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:54.180 --> 00:23:57.960
world affected by that trauma, having time to&nbsp;
process that trauma -- and that's a specific&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:57.960 --> 00:24:02.460
and immediate traumatic event in the community of&nbsp;
Haddonfield -- but then they also had a worldwide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:06.660
pandemic and peculiar politics and another million&nbsp;
things that turned their world upside down.”

00:24:06.660 --> 00:24:10.560
This statement made it seem like the movie&nbsp;
was actually going to acknowledge COVID-19,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:10.560 --> 00:24:14.940
and to be fair, it does acknowledge it.&nbsp;
Despite the virus breaking out in late 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:14.940 --> 00:24:19.260
it didn’t begin to affect life in the United&nbsp;
States until 2020. The opening with Corey and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:19.260 --> 00:24:23.760
Jeremy took place in October 2019, and we see a&nbsp;
montage of anguish during subsequent Halloweens.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:23.760 --> 00:24:28.860
As a side note, this montage contains a really&nbsp;
dark detail. We see the mother of Oscar Berlucci,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:28.860 --> 00:24:33.480
one of the victims in 2018, hanging in a devil&nbsp;
costume, the same outfit her son died in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:33.480 --> 00:24:37.560
almost as if to suggest that she was overcome&nbsp;
with grief and decided she could not go on.

00:24:37.560 --> 00:24:42.300
But we also see this crime scene in a Jeep, where&nbsp;
the coroner and crime scene photographer are both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:42.300 --> 00:24:46.440
wearing masks, suggesting that this probably&nbsp;
happened in October of 2020. But this is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:46.440 --> 00:24:50.580
only evidence in the movie that the pandemic&nbsp;
began. So what did Gordon-Green mean when he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:50.580 --> 00:24:54.480
said that the people of Haddonfield had their&nbsp;
world turned upside down by a worldwide pandemic?

00:24:54.480 --> 00:24:58.320
I don’t believe he ever meant that COVID would&nbsp;
be at the forefront of the story, but rather,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:58.320 --> 00:25:02.160
it seems to be a big part of the subtext.&nbsp;
Laurie’s whole character arc in this movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:02.160 --> 00:25:06.180
is about learning to move on from a traumatic&nbsp;
event. She had to deal with 50-some people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:06.180 --> 00:25:09.960
including her own daughter, getting killed&nbsp;
after she tried to warn everybody about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:09.960 --> 00:25:13.800
threat that was Michael Myers, and nobody&nbsp;
listened. It sounds a lot like the countless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:13.800 --> 00:25:17.760
healthcare professionals who tried to sound&nbsp;
the alarm about COVID-19. Nobody listened,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:17.760 --> 00:25:20.940
6.5 million people were killed,&nbsp;
and that number is still rising.

00:25:20.940 --> 00:25:24.060
Throughout my Halloween Things You Missed&nbsp;
series, I’ve talked about how many Halloween&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:24.060 --> 00:25:28.080
films reflect the culture of the time period&nbsp;
they were made in. Halloween Ends is no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:28.080 --> 00:25:31.980
different. There’s never been a more impactful&nbsp;
event in our lifetimes, and in this movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:31.980 --> 00:25:36.240
Michael Myers serves as a stand-in instigator for&nbsp;
the collective grief we’ve all been dealing with.

00:25:36.240 --> 00:25:40.620
In fact, there are many instances where Michael&nbsp;
is compared to a virus. There are constant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:40.620 --> 00:25:45.120
worries about being “infected” and his evil is&nbsp;
literally referred to as being “contagious.”

00:25:46.157 --> 00:25:51.777
– [Laurie] The suffering Michael&nbsp;
caused became an infection, passing onto people who never even crossed his path.

00:25:51.777 --> 00:25:54.420
– [Corey] It’s contagious, right?
– [Laurie] The other kind of evil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:54.420 --> 00:25:58.522
lives inside us. Like a sickness, or an infection.

00:25:58.522 --> 00:26:02.580
– We even see characters trying to spin ridiculous&nbsp;
narratives, like the idea that Michael was an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:02.580 --> 00:26:06.600
innocent mental patient that Laurie pushed too&nbsp;
far, causing him to snap. By the time of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:06.600 --> 00:26:10.380
movie, everyone seems desperate to blame&nbsp;
something for hurt that Michael caused.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:10.380 --> 00:26:14.220
Did it come from a bat? Was it leaked from&nbsp;
a lab? Does it really matter at this point?

00:26:14.220 --> 00:26:17.880
Laurie is our protagonist, and she is trying&nbsp;
to learn to deal with the consequences of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:17.880 --> 00:26:21.300
Michael Myers. It’s all about this self&nbsp;
promise of hers, she’s trying not to let&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:21.300 --> 00:26:25.380
fear rule her life anymore. She still has&nbsp;
some safety precautions, as one should,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:25.380 --> 00:26:29.340
but for the first time, we see her trying to get&nbsp;
back to normal, putting up Halloween decorations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:29.340 --> 00:26:32.640
carving pumpkins, and not spending&nbsp;
all of her time preparing to fight.

00:26:32.640 --> 00:26:36.420
She does all of this, despite it being generally&nbsp;
accepted that Michael is still out there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:36.420 --> 00:26:39.540
and at times, we see her panic and&nbsp;
revert back to the Laurie we saw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:39.540 --> 00:26:43.440
in 2018. Her journey in this movie&nbsp;
is trying to fully overcome that.

00:26:43.440 --> 00:26:47.280
That’s why I find the ambiguous ending&nbsp;
regarding the fate of Corey Cunningham to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:47.280 --> 00:26:51.180
be kind of interesting. Near the end of the&nbsp;
movie, we see that Corey has the ability to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:51.180 --> 00:26:54.960
recover from would-be fatal injuries, like&nbsp;
Michael does, and we never see what happens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:54.960 --> 00:26:59.280
to Corey. There are many scenes that imply&nbsp;
that evil is part of a continuous cycle. Even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:59.280 --> 00:27:03.360
if you find a way to defeat Michael Myers,&nbsp;
there is always a new evil on the horizon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:03.360 --> 00:27:06.960
whether it’s Corey, or one of the other&nbsp;
deplorable characters in Haddonfield.

00:27:06.960 --> 00:27:10.920
Right from the get go, the opening credits&nbsp;
this time show us a series of jack o’lanterns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:10.920 --> 00:27:14.760
being born out of other jack o’lanterns,&nbsp;
representing the cycle of evil being reborn.

00:27:14.760 --> 00:27:17.760
In one scene, Lindsey does a&nbsp;
tarot card reading for Allyson.

00:27:17.760 --> 00:27:21.660
– [Allyson] Oh no, I got the death card.
– No, that’s not bad in tarot. No,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:21.660 --> 00:27:25.320
that just means a major phase is&nbsp;
ending an a new one is about to begin.

00:27:25.320 --> 00:27:28.860
– It seems to be talking about Allyson&nbsp;
starting a new relationship with Corey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:28.860 --> 00:27:31.560
but in the grand context of the&nbsp;
movie, it’s talking about one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:31.560 --> 00:27:34.740
phase of evil ending with Michael,&nbsp;
and a new one beginning in Corey.

00:27:34.740 --> 00:27:37.020
A similar theme is expressed in Laurie’s writing.

00:27:37.020 --> 00:27:38.880
– I'm hopeful, with perspective,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:38.880 --> 00:27:44.040
that my experience will help others heal.&nbsp;
You have to ask yourself, "Am I in control,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:44.040 --> 00:27:49.440
"or do the elements control me?” Life&nbsp;
or death. Suicide or cherry blossoms?

00:27:49.440 --> 00:27:54.000
– [Zac] Cherry blossoms in Japanese culture are the&nbsp;
symbolic flower of the spring, a time of renewal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:54.000 --> 00:27:58.320
and the fleeting nature of life. We can literally&nbsp;
see the cycle repeating itself in the movie. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:58.320 --> 00:28:02.280
old Myers house is demolished, but there just&nbsp;
ends up being a new horror house in Haddonfield,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:02.280 --> 00:28:05.880
when the Allen house is abandoned after&nbsp;
Jeremy’s untimely death. But I think,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:05.880 --> 00:28:10.680
whether we are talking about COVID or Michael&nbsp;
Myers, the end of Laurie’s memoir puts it best.

00:28:10.680 --> 00:28:16.260
– I’ve said goodbye to my boogeyman. But the&nbsp;
truth is, evil doesn’t die. It changes shape.

00:28:16.260 --> 00:28:19.020
– And with that, I have analyzed&nbsp;
everything you might have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:19.020 --> 00:28:23.160
missed in the Halloween franchise.&nbsp;
Except for the Rob Zombie duology,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:23.160 --> 00:28:26.700
which I skipped over. I think Jimmy Champane&nbsp;
and I will cover those next Halloween.

00:28:26.700 --> 00:28:31.500
The playlist on the left is my full collection of&nbsp;
episodes on the Halloween franchise, and if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:31.500 --> 00:28:36.120
love horror, I cover all kinds of horror on this&nbsp;
channel. Make sure you subscribe to CZsWorld, ring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:36.120 --> 00:28:42.000
the deathbell for notifications and I will see&nbsp;
you in the next one. Assuming, we both survive.

00:28:42.226 --> 00:28:44.226
(spooky dance music)

